    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d97">

                <pb facs="0137" n="113" sameAs="frus:frus1864p4/pg113"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Motley.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 99.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1864-10-15"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 15, 1864</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I call your attention to the enclosed copy
                    of a despatch from M. A. Jackson, United States consul at Halifax, and of an
                    extract from a late Charleston paper, by which it was accompanied, in regard to
                    the proposed building in Europe of a number of fast-sailing steamers for the
                    purpose of running the blockade of Wilmington with troops from Poland to the
                    number of thirty thousand. You will exercise your usual vigilance towards
                    thwarting the scheme referred to.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Lothrop Motley</hi>, Esq., &amp;<hi
                            rendition="#italic">c</hi>., &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.,
                            &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.<hi rendition="#italic">,
                            Vienna.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
